estion.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7909e3f4-0551-5a81-bb90-5294c3520132"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7909e3f4-0551-5a81-bb90-5294c3520132" :answer-field/id #uuid "7909e3f4-0551-5a81-bb90-5294c3520132" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-632d51ed-4a23-51ff-9d48-6ce5aa233692" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e64f8c14-477c-56bd-9fd5-c19d06da2274" "answer-be0842e6-8ca5-5031-a47d-2b3064c0239e" "answer-86e62df7-794b-5d7c-8bee-a589fa6c1111" "answer-632d51ed-4a23-51ff-9d48-6ce5aa233692" "answer-2449df29-abd1-5cbe-8586-d027021dd009"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e64f8c14-477c-56bd-9fd5-c19d06da2274" :answer/id #uuid "e64f8c14-477c-56bd-9fd5-c19d06da2274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{0,1,2,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be0842e6-8ca5-5031-a47d-2b3064c0239e" :answer/id #uuid "be0842e6-8ca5-5031-a47d-2b3064c0239e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{0,12,24…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86e62df7-794b-5d7c-8bee-a589fa6c1111" :answer/id #uuid "86e62df7-794b-5d7c-8bee-a589fa6c1111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{0,3,6…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-632d51ed-4a23-51ff-9d48-6ce5aa233692" :answer/id #uuid "632d51ed-4a23-51ff-9d48-6ce5aa233692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{0,6,12…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2449df29-abd1-5cbe-8586-d027021dd009" :answer/id #uuid "2449df29-abd1-5cbe-8586-d027021dd009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{0,3,6,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186399111 :question/problem "If $X=\\{1,3,5,…,99\\}$, which collection of subsets of $X$ is a partition of $X?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,99\\},\\{2,4,6,…,98\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{41,43,45,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,69\\},\\{70,71,72,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $70$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,39\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) do not appear in any subsets." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186399112 :answer-field/correct "answer-ca09aba2-3580-5133-877c-ffc90b4818be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0abebf23-9e34-5073-997c-2ff3939d5d53" "answer-148bd622-db85-5a90-9ee3-bd939e2f6110" "answer-ca09aba2-3580-5133-877c-ffc90b4818be" "answer-87279b1e-9a8b-56d8-876e-fed29939ffba" "answer-d63996f1-74f9-55d5-b8bc-f0b6fb5dcd73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0abebf23-9e34-5073-997c-2ff3939d5d53" :answer/id #uuid "0abebf23-9e34-5073-997c-2ff3939d5d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{1,3,5,…,39\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-148bd622-db85-5a90-9ee3-bd939e2f6110" :answer/id #uuid "148bd622-db85-5a90-9ee3-bd939e2f6110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{41,43,45,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca09aba2-3580-5133-877c-ffc90b4818be" :answer/id #uuid "ca09aba2-3580-5133-877c-ffc90b4818be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87279b1e-9a8b-56d8-876e-fed29939ffba" :answer/id #uuid "87279b1e-9a8b-56d8-876e-fed29939ffba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{1,3,5,…,69\\},\\{70,71,72,…,99\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d63996f1-74f9-55d5-b8bc-f0b6fb5dcd73" :answer/id #uuid "d63996f1-74f9-55d5-b8bc-f0b6fb5dcd73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{1,3,5,…,99\\},\\{2,4,6,…,98\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186417774 :question/problem "If $Y=\\{20,22,24,…,180\\},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{20,22,24,…,60\\},\\{62,64,66,…,120\\},\\{122,124,126,…,180\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{\\{20,22,24,…,70\\},\\{140,142,144,…,180\\}\\}$ is not a partition because some elements of $Y,$ such as $72,74,…,138,$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{20,22,24,…,80\\},\\{66,68,70,…,180\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the elements $66,68,…,80$ appear in both subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,180\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $2,4,…,20,$ that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- $\\{\\{20,22,24,26\\},\\{27,28,29,…,180\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $27$ and $29,$ that do not appear in $Y.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186417771 :answer-field/correct "answer-90fb221a-f525-5551-a4e2-e7ab19047d2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5aa759dd-5b09-57af-8099-171ff4cbcde8" "answer-a58aef66-b4ae-59a0-a9df-95a3da99f424" "answer-90fb221a-f525-5551-a4e2-e7ab19047d2f" "answer-c962addc-6fe6-5b22-82f1-c219761dcdc9" "answer-a1b65d64-7626-5243-8360-4705024e70ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aa759dd-5b09-57af-8099-171ff4cbcde8" :answer/id #uuid "5aa759dd-5b09-57af-8099-171ff4cbcde8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{2,4,6,…,180\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a58aef66-b4ae-59a0-a9df-95a3da99f424" :answer/id #uuid "a58aef66-b4ae-59a0-a9df-95a3da99f424" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{20,22,24,26\\},\\{27,28,29,…,180\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90fb221a-f525-5551-a4e2-e7ab19047d2f" :answer/id #uuid "90fb221a-f525-5551-a4e2-e7ab19047d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{20,22,24,…,60\\},\\{62,64,66,…,120\\},\\{122,124,126,…,180\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c962addc-6fe6-5b22-82f1-c219761dcdc9" :answer/id #uuid "c962addc-6fe6-5b22-82f1-c219761dcdc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{20,22,24,…,70\\},\\{140,142,144,…,180\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1b65d64-7626-5243-8360-4705024e70ed" :answer/id #uuid "a1b65d64-7626-5243-8360-4705024e70ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\{20,22,24,…,80\\},\\{66,68,70,…,180\\}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060958 :tutorial/content "A **partition** of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nIn other words, none of the subsets can be the null set $(\\emptyset),$ and every element of $A$ must be contained in one *and only one* subset.\n\nFor example, the following collections of subsets of $X=\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ are all partitions:\n\n- $X_1 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_2 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_3 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_4 = \\{ \\{ 1, 4, 5\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_5 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4\\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n\nHowever, the following collections are *not* partitions:\n\n- $X_6 = \\{ \\{ 1\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$ - the number $2$ is not included in any subset\n\n- $X_7 = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - includes $\\emptyset$\n\n- $X_8 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - the number $3$ is included in two different subsets\n\n- $X_9 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2 \\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$ - missing $4$ and $5,$ and $2$ is included in two different subsets\n\n- $X_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\}$ - this not a collection of subsets" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059918 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186067750 :answer-field/choices 17592186067751] [:db/retract 17592186067750 :answer-field/choices 17592186067752] [:db/retract 17592186067750 :answer-field/choices 17592186067753] [:db/retract 17592186067750 :answer-field/choices 17592186067754] [:db/retract 17592186067750 :answer-field/choices 17592186067755] {:db/id 17592186068681 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b9bd4bfd-1d1e-5b71-9461-1eac5c12f4bb" "question-b4c8a987-ad34-580a-aa0f-6a58f6c286c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068542 :question/problem "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a diameter of $d=10?$ \n\n![](images/b1/b1ebd81fca9688b5688dc916d6be62bad14853f55a8e66c5c7af469dd4032ec4.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=\\pi d$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the exact answer. If we want an approximate answer, say rounded to three decimal places, we can use the approximation $\\pi\\approx 3.14\\,159,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =10\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & ≈10\\cdot 3.14\\,159 \\\\  & ≈31.416.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068682 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19bc1142-df4b-536a-85ea-0b9c7ee4c94e" "question-1630b08d-aa50-5fe7-9faa-2b7a697c8eb6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068543 :question/problem "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a radius of $6?$\n\n![](images/3c/3c21021529285f488ca794a442e5826a033ed2a4c6f4fad53ab9e8fdc84d35ee.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068683 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1d3f49ce-877b-5ae1-8337-866d03e886d7" "question-6a8defe9-ca28-57be-8b44-d4ab01b2ecd4" "question-c2fe80a7-5526-5b19-979f-2b18ba9fc425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068544 :question/problem "What is the radius $r$ of a circle with a circumference of $C=17\\pi?$\n\n![](images/69/697cc9ca06bcfe46d84dfab74e0f6ae83f4342607ea4af138b111606c16e8a03.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=2\\pi r$ and solve for $r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 17\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068684 :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0394adcb-093f-5edf-94a5-7360ea14bac2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068545 :question/problem "Carol has to wrap a rope around a circular column whose diameter is $20\\,\\textrm{cm}.$ What length of the rope will wrap the column perfectly?" :question/worked-solution "The length of the rope needed to wrap around the column is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C = \\pi d$, where $d=20\\,\\textrm{cm}$ is the diameter. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC = \\pi\\cdot 20 = 20\\pi \\,\\textrm{cm}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9bd4bfd-1d1e-5b71-9461-1eac5c12f4bb" :question/id #uuid "b9bd4bfd-1d1e-5b71-9461-1eac5c12f4bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-75767" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c88f19b18c77ae8473dbfb055518ab88558b03f2d20a169e548e034b67cb621e.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a diameter of $4\\,\\text{ft}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=\\pi d$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13dcb38d-75b8-5346-be9e-8fa946583030"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13dcb38d-75b8-5346-be9e-8fa946583030" :answer-field/id #uuid "13dcb38d-75b8-5346-be9e-8fa946583030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3587083-4a83-5f99-8f5c-e94ac28701e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c49943b6-764e-5732-8324-7cb3a112bb0c" "answer-d26958e7-a612-5fea-82c8-891b3f04d457" "answer-a3587083-4a83-5f99-8f5c-e94ac28701e6" "answer-6dc71b3a-2ec5-5ed8-a8b8-61586b1fb737" "answer-66c7e13f-2309-5bd4-a87e-93583b67f16e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c49943b6-764e-5732-8324-7cb3a112bb0c" :answer/id #uuid "c49943b6-764e-5732-8324-7cb3a112bb0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d26958e7-a612-5fea-82c8-891b3f04d457" :answer/id #uuid "d26958e7-a612-5fea-82c8-891b3f04d457" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\pi \\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3587083-4a83-5f99-8f5c-e94ac28701e6" :answer/id #uuid "a3587083-4a83-5f99-8f5c-e94ac28701e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dc71b3a-2ec5-5ed8-a8b8-61586b1fb737" :answer/id #uuid "6dc71b3a-2ec5-5ed8-a8b8-61586b1fb737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\pi }^{2}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66c7e13f-2309-5bd4-a87e-93583b67f16e" :answer/id #uuid "66c7e13f-2309-5bd4-a87e-93583b67f16e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi \\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4c8a987-ad34-580a-aa0f-6a58f6c286c7" :question/id #uuid "b4c8a987-ad34-580a-aa0f-6a58f6c286c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-122010" :question/problem "![](images/92/92d75539c4e6e721349f78850a7c69e875d9c5415cbbad18592924d0ae66383e.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a diameter of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }\\,\\text{yd}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=\\pi d$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc7cc937-333c-5443-91a2-63cd88fc55b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc7cc937-333c-5443-91a2-63cd88fc55b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc7cc937-333c-5443-91a2-63cd88fc55b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3298fbad-dfc7-588e-b38c-20a57b427c71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3fcbb64-00a4-5a80-9e45-f3d6169aad66" "answer-b043737b-735c-537e-a961-a9037a95c0a0" "answer-c18793f8-6949-5175-b11f-dd92927bff74" "answer-3298fbad-dfc7-588e-b38c-20a57b427c71" "answer-da58eae1-89a7-5eb3-86f6-078a9166659a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3fcbb64-00a4-5a80-9e45-f3d6169aad66" :answer/id #uuid "e3fcbb64-00a4-5a80-9e45-f3d6169aad66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b043737b-735c-537e-a961-a9037a95c0a0" :answer/id #uuid "b043737b-735c-537e-a961-a9037a95c0a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c18793f8-6949-5175-b11f-dd92927bff74" :answer/id #uuid "c18793f8-6949-5175-b11f-dd92927bff74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3298fbad-dfc7-588e-b38c-20a57b427c71" :answer/id #uuid "3298fbad-dfc7-588e-b38c-20a57b427c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da58eae1-89a7-5eb3-86f6-078a9166659a" :answer/id #uuid "da58eae1-89a7-5eb3-86f6-078a9166659a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-19bc1142-df4b-536a-85ea-0b9c7ee4c94e" :question/id #uuid "19bc1142-df4b-536a-85ea-0b9c7ee4c94e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75773" :question/problem "![](images/73/73c890f1181c0073c0f56c31c8343872d5ad31e71b7a5755ea1633f52934a451.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a radius of $r=4?$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8\\pi  \\\\  & ≈25.133,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99b743c8-67a7-5feb-bfaf-2c8a980270f9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99b743c8-67a7-5feb-bfaf-2c8a980270f9" :answer-field/id #uuid "99b743c8-67a7-5feb-bfaf-2c8a980270f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-43206200-e244-522b-8a72-991d693ed87f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da581d39-ef69-5213-90fb-8c91419c2f57" "answer-d67cc499-894e-5988-bd69-06d2c94e7e94" "answer-43206200-e244-522b-8a72-991d693ed87f" "answer-e2e18c30-7e2a-5bbb-9f3f-061e84bf85cd" "answer-e71c90f9-8d41-5724-a6c3-602bba111e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da581d39-ef69-5213-90fb-8c91419c2f57" :answer/id #uuid "da581d39-ef69-5213-90fb-8c91419c2f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.131" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d67cc499-894e-5988-bd69-06d2c94e7e94" :answer/id #uuid "d67cc499-894e-5988-bd69-06d2c94e7e94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.333" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43206200-e244-522b-8a72-991d693ed87f" :answer/id #uuid "43206200-e244-522b-8a72-991d693ed87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.133" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2e18c30-7e2a-5bbb-9f3f-061e84bf85cd" :answer/id #uuid "e2e18c30-7e2a-5bbb-9f3f-061e84bf85cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26.130" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e71c90f9-8d41-5724-a6c3-602bba111e4c" :answer/id #uuid "e71c90f9-8d41-5724-a6c3-602bba111e4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27.111" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1630b08d-aa50-5fe7-9faa-2b7a697c8eb6" :question/id #uuid "1630b08d-aa50-5fe7-9faa-2b7a697c8eb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122016" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bf0d8b99d9c681a6537aaeae828687719ac994766ce6d6322b50502e4fadef71.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a radius of $13\\,\\text{mm}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 13 \\\\  & =26\\pi \\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0c1a118e-d653-5ade-a60a-f9eb1a92c38e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0c1a118e-d653-5ade-a60a-f9eb1a92c38e" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c1a118e-d653-5ade-a60a-f9eb1a92c38e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48c20b0a-8d49-5eaa-8750-94833a24e985" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7e42224-c964-5185-8f33-87c66ceacb9f" "answer-48c20b0a-8d49-5eaa-8750-94833a24e985" "answer-3a8ea297-e4d4-516d-8dc1-7b49c0605fbd" "answer-dd2f71e4-3d3d-5c3a-b1b0-c09c3686c042" "answer-353ecedb-ffe8-5507-8cab-094996e37191"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7e42224-c964-5185-8f33-87c66ceacb9f" :answer/id #uuid "e7e42224-c964-5185-8f33-87c66ceacb9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\pi \\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48c20b0a-8d49-5eaa-8750-94833a24e985" :answer/id #uuid "48c20b0a-8d49-5eaa-8750-94833a24e985" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26\\pi \\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a8ea297-e4d4-516d-8dc1-7b49c0605fbd" :answer/id #uuid "3a8ea297-e4d4-516d-8dc1-7b49c0605fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.14\\pi \\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd2f71e4-3d3d-5c3a-b1b0-c09c3686c042" :answer/id #uuid "dd2f71e4-3d3d-5c3a-b1b0-c09c3686c042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{\\pi }\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-353ecedb-ffe8-5507-8cab-094996e37191" :answer/id #uuid "353ecedb-ffe8-5507-8cab-094996e37191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{26}{\\pi }\\,\\text{mm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d3f49ce-877b-5ae1-8337-866d03e886d7" :question/id #uuid "1d3f49ce-877b-5ae1-8337-866d03e886d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-3735" :question/problem "![](images/57/5782df9eb0a0055ef071647a133bf6cadf7c5121a160a4ffe2383efa899535e0.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle with a circumference of $12\\pi \\,\\text{ft}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=\\pi d$ and solve for $d.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\ 12\\pi  & =\\pi d \\\\ d & =\\frac{12\\pi }{\\pi } \\\\ d & =12\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-975c17ad-d8c3-5189-bedc-fac0a72dbaf4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-975c17ad-d8c3-5189-bedc-fac0a72dbaf4" :answer-field/id #uuid "975c17ad-d8c3-5189-bedc-fac0a72dbaf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" "answer-a5a03208-6893-5823-b472-bde68ebd603b" "answer-a01f82a3-a3b2-562a-a714-110588418699" "answer-5c369159-c893-5584-a4e8-d9c17c11c023" "answer-12d8fbfd-f3db-53ff-b98a-0cff0ed19456"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" :answer/id #uuid "cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5a03208-6893-5823-b472-bde68ebd603b" :answer/id #uuid "a5a03208-6893-5823-b472-bde68ebd603b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a01f82a3-a3b2-562a-a714-110588418699" :answer/id #uuid "a01f82a3-a3b2-562a-a714-110588418699" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c369159-c893-5584-a4e8-d9c17c11c023" :answer/id #uuid "5c369159-c893-5584-a4e8-d9c17c11c023" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi \\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12d8fbfd-f3db-53ff-b98a-0cff0ed19456" :answer/id #uuid "12d8fbfd-f3db-53ff-b98a-0cff0ed19456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a8defe9-ca28-57be-8b44-d4ab01b2ecd4" :question/id #uuid "6a8defe9-ca28-57be-8b44-d4ab01b2ecd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122023" :question/problem "![](images/a8/a83fd5135d18ff095a601f6ff09658c1ce6ab877fe5004e62761dc93f530a624.png)\n\nWhat is the radius $r$ of a circle with a circumference of $7\\,\\text{m}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=2\\pi r$ and solve for $r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 7 & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =\\frac{7}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24ad6743-0f7a-5c97-9471-a63ef037cbb8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24ad6743-0f7a-5c97-9471-a63ef037cbb8" :answer-field/id #uuid "24ad6743-0f7a-5c97-9471-a63ef037cbb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-524ca655-89ad-5837-b4d2-54ff11222e1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d986cc0-80fc-5ceb-95fd-65978a21dfa4" "answer-5988d876-d3b9-5f05-b0eb-c2064ceb4b6e" "answer-191fe382-697d-5b7c-8ec0-e8fe5d495c3f" "answer-524ca655-89ad-5837-b4d2-54ff11222e1d" "answer-223d7eda-c9fb-5a5e-9401-5a640838ce42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d986cc0-80fc-5ceb-95fd-65978a21dfa4" :answer/id #uuid "4d986cc0-80fc-5ceb-95fd-65978a21dfa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5988d876-d3b9-5f05-b0eb-c2064ceb4b6e" :answer/id #uuid "5988d876-d3b9-5f05-b0eb-c2064ceb4b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-191fe382-697d-5b7c-8ec0-e8fe5d495c3f" :answer/id #uuid "191fe382-697d-5b7c-8ec0-e8fe5d495c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-524ca655-89ad-5837-b4d2-54ff11222e1d" :answer/id #uuid "524ca655-89ad-5837-b4d2-54ff11222e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-223d7eda-c9fb-5a5e-9401-5a640838ce42" :answer/id #uuid "223d7eda-c9fb-5a5e-9401-5a640838ce42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4\\pi }\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c2fe80a7-5526-5b19-979f-2b18ba9fc425" :question/id #uuid "c2fe80a7-5526-5b19-979f-2b18ba9fc425" :question/math-academy-id "q-122032" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e046aafb09255a579c76a48f0f422627761a19451ae36a053424a8ac8a3332f7.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle with a circumference of $\\frac{5\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=\\pi d$ and solve for $d.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{2} & =\\pi d \\\\ d & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\ d & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f9626a0-67b1-590b-90d1-2f7438f67929"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f9626a0-67b1-590b-90d1-2f7438f67929" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f9626a0-67b1-590b-90d1-2f7438f67929" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f31ae9f-7d96-5240-9377-5f2c2a8bd26c" "answer-08702ecd-ba2a-5dc4-a61b-587184515899" "answer-10c4a483-8085-5d16-911c-be7f848c5f52" "answer-5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" "answer-45d9e406-7f39-5af9-87d1-244fdbdd4f03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f31ae9f-7d96-5240-9377-5f2c2a8bd26c" :answer/id #uuid "9f31ae9f-7d96-5240-9377-5f2c2a8bd26c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08702ecd-ba2a-5dc4-a61b-587184515899" :answer/id #uuid "08702ecd-ba2a-5dc4-a61b-587184515899" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10c4a483-8085-5d16-911c-be7f848c5f52" :answer/id #uuid "10c4a483-8085-5d16-911c-be7f848c5f52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" :answer/id #uuid "5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45d9e406-7f39-5af9-87d1-244fdbdd4f03" :answer/id #uuid "45d9e406-7f39-5af9-87d1-244fdbdd4f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069430 :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad42b4bd62bf64e1ac086a60ace286b3e6d1c136f423d2ae6aabf6339cea9071.png)\n\nWhat length of fence is needed to border a circular plot of land with a diameter of $30\\,\\text{m}?$" :question/worked-solution "The length of the fence needed to border the circular land is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=30\\,\\text{m}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 30=30\\pi \\,\\text{m}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067750 :answer-field/correct "answer-95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f59a7da9-9cf4-567a-b2b9-156ace337242" "answer-d1913280-fe19-5501-8536-b0d76434a0a0" "answer-95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" "answer-e48372d3-e37a-5407-a1ff-e01f1204dac3" "answer-96ace683-1432-5b37-90f5-77548e014d86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f59a7da9-9cf4-567a-b2b9-156ace337242" :answer/id #uuid "f59a7da9-9cf4-567a-b2b9-156ace337242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1913280-fe19-5501-8536-b0d76434a0a0" :answer/id #uuid "d1913280-fe19-5501-8536-b0d76434a0a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" :answer/id #uuid "95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e48372d3-e37a-5407-a1ff-e01f1204dac3" :answer/id #uuid "e48372d3-e37a-5407-a1ff-e01f1204dac3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96ace683-1432-5b37-90f5-77548e014d86" :answer/id #uuid "96ace683-1432-5b37-90f5-77548e014d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0394adcb-093f-5edf-94a5-7360ea14bac2" :question/id #uuid "0394adcb-093f-5edf-94a5-7360ea14bac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-53554" :question/problem "![](images/43/43818f663454fe239d4b881a7cbd2f469391e80d87246a145f0fe1d294c9f71a.png)\n\nWhat length of chain will perfectly wrap around a circular tree trunk with a diameter of $2\\,\\text{yd}?$" :question/worked-solution "The length of the chain needed to wrap around the tree is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=2\\,\\text{yd}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 2=2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a0f286f-12e5-5f1b-bf30-8442ae915046"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a0f286f-12e5-5f1b-bf30-8442ae915046" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0f286f-12e5-5f1b-bf30-8442ae915046" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-983e66cd-9dd5-5e32-86f0-ba0838837e94" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec0637c9-f8bd-5b9d-8dfe-080612467a2d" "answer-983e66cd-9dd5-5e32-86f0-ba0838837e94" "answer-ac14585a-95cc-5525-b26d-ec79bfbcf958" "answer-7a2abbe0-b911-5ed0-b8cb-f6c69ce3381b" "answer-bd70ba3b-bf04-5a41-8caf-b025691f64f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec0637c9-f8bd-5b9d-8dfe-080612467a2d" :answer/id #uuid "ec0637c9-f8bd-5b9d-8dfe-080612467a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-983e66cd-9dd5-5e32-86f0-ba0838837e94" :answer/id #uuid "983e66cd-9dd5-5e32-86f0-ba0838837e94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac14585a-95cc-5525-b26d-ec79bfbcf958" :answer/id #uuid "ac14585a-95cc-5525-b26d-ec79bfbcf958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a2abbe0-b911-5ed0-b8cb-f6c69ce3381b" :answer/id #uuid "7a2abbe0-b911-5ed0-b8cb-f6c69ce3381b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd70ba3b-bf04-5a41-8caf-b025691f64f6" :answer/id #uuid "bd70ba3b-bf04-5a41-8caf-b025691f64f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069956 :tutorial/content "The **circumference** of a circle is the length of the path that goes around the circle.\n\n![](images/ac/ac8f31a99961c51cb53695d9daab017126d1316b720e6383b876824d7c7947bd.png)\n\nThe circumference is usually denoted by the letter $C.$\n\nOne important fact about the circumference is that, for *any* circle, no matter how small or large it is, the ratio of circumference $C$ to diameter $d$ is a fixed number! Specifically,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{C}{d} = {\\color{blue}\\boldsymbol{\\pi}} \\approx 3.141\\,592\\,654...\n$$\n\n \n\nThis important irrational number is called **pi** (pronounced \"pie\") and we use the Greek letter $\\pi$ to express it. So, we can calculate the circumference by using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\pi d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, our circle has diameter $4\\,\\textrm{cm},$ so its circumference is\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\cdot 4 = 4\\pi \\approx 12.566\\,\\mathrm{cm},\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal digits.\n\nSince the diameter is twice as long as the radius ($d=2r$), we can also write the formula for the circumference as\n\n$$\nC = \\pi d = 2\\pi r.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-a14139c8-87eb-5e69-a268-c7cb088cf812" :tutorial/id #uuid "a14139c8-87eb-5e69-a268-c7cb088cf812" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15549 :tutorial/title "Calculating the Length of a Part of a Circle" :tutorial/content "The problem of finding the length of a circle or a part of a circle often appears in real life. \n\nFor example, consider the pie in the shape of a circle divided into six equal slices, as shown in the figure below.\n\n![](images/48/48b416b9dffbf6e3e746e3fa8f90ec8043f937fe612e36e1219b5e9e8c368f22.png)\n\n How to find the total length of the border of one slice of pie?\n\nThe border of the slice of pie will consist of two parts:\n\n- the top and the bottom parts, which consist of two radii;\n\n- the right part (circular part), which consists of one-sixth of the circumference.\n\nFirst, let's find the length of the circular part. The formula for the circumference of a circle is ![](images/63/636374af24eb4d5c435de97b8e1ac460148deba4916b0954e3d1d2f7a364f9d7.svg) where ![](images/31/3122e2ea79ab0512edfce5c875a099de1a7067581b658d1b8fc9c105277aed36.svg) is the radius. Therefore, we have \n![](images/15/15bff81cb45d3df680e782e69534d2489388dfbcfd12b3cd579298d03f8bd452.svg)\n\nFinally, the length of the border is\n![](images/15/15037adbdea6b21d54991917b5dad6108c60257fd8f509300642343a101ebeeb.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068987 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :activity/steps ["step-cc9d4179-5034-59aa-b0e6-47636130b8db"] :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069550 :step/next "step-cc9d4179-5034-59aa-b0e6-47636130b8db" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cc9d4179-5034-59aa-b0e6-47636130b8db" :step/id #uuid "cc9d4179-5034-59aa-b0e6-47636130b8db" :step/content "tutorial-a14139c8-87eb-5e69-a268-c7cb088cf812" :step/math-academy-id 643569 :step/next 17592186069551 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186217800 :question/answer-fields 17592186216667] [:db/retract 17592186216668 :answer-field/choices 17592186216672] [:db/retract 17592186216668 :answer-field/choices 17592186216670] {:db/id 17592186217244 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-25dddbef-ad84-5535-a187-268eebd173d8" "question-d2c79c80-99de-54b9-9d82-c2f07cd702f0" "question-32e7120e-ecd0-54a1-8649-0fea9e5b153d" "question-64a84975-134c-59e7-b3de-faa7ec811813" "question-753b45d7-da51-5748-9817-073e29597daf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186217245 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-53cebc23-dff1-56fe-a57a-9a0d9ca25a96" "question-fa87e239-f514-5ab3-af2e-43a62163086f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186217246 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e6daeb8c-1b8f-5fdd-ab26-f055c20928ce" "question-c5f06778-8fd3-5821-8bf0-21b9cd17fe6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186217005 :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if $y_1$ and $y_2$ are solutions of\n\n$$\ny''+P(x)y'+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\nW'(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of $y'$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\nW'(x)= \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{-4}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-4W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-4x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-4x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=-3$ to find $C{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-4\\cdot 2} \\\\ -3 & =C{e}^{-8} \\\\ C & =-3{e}^{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=-3e^{8}e^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nSince $-3e^{8}e^{-4x}\\neq 0$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, we conclude that ![](images/d5/d526e46960ff276b3249961ad4939cb2ac2f84fd2dba97644df92b96972dc36e.svg)\n\nSo, $y_1$ and $y_2$ are ![](images/83/8387c02793e59a20c3c126da147ca4b1f6812e11f0173eed6e1768be85a07f7d.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-25dddbef-ad84-5535-a187-268eebd173d8" :question/id #uuid "25dddbef-ad84-5535-a187-268eebd173d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-343263" :question/problem "$$\n4x{y}^{″}+({x}^{2}-8){y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?\n\n$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in standard form. Since $x>0$, we can divide both sides by $4x$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{{x}^{2}-8}{4x}{y}^{′}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{4x}y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-8}{4x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{x}{4})W(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0dfaec97-3c0a-5f5b-9b6f-70e8a9d7277c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0dfaec97-3c0a-5f5b-9b6f-70e8a9d7277c" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfaec97-3c0a-5f5b-9b6f-70e8a9d7277c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b15944cc-b6d7-5607-bb8a-096b5d8506b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b15944cc-b6d7-5607-bb8a-096b5d8506b2" "answer-57522148-92ca-5be5-9f64-7d028cd0d2cb" "answer-29e9f80a-809c-565a-8d3e-f30a614ba078" "answer-6df2da19-269f-5bba-a866-2d28fc031ec6" "answer-65a0e4ce-bd6e-5296-8a0a-5fd18bf74b74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b15944cc-b6d7-5607-bb8a-096b5d8506b2" :answer/id #uuid "b15944cc-b6d7-5607-bb8a-096b5d8506b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{x}{4})W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57522148-92ca-5be5-9f64-7d028cd0d2cb" :answer/id #uuid "57522148-92ca-5be5-9f64-7d028cd0d2cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{2}{x})W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29e9f80a-809c-565a-8d3e-f30a614ba078" :answer/id #uuid "29e9f80a-809c-565a-8d3e-f30a614ba078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{4}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6df2da19-269f-5bba-a866-2d28fc031ec6" :answer/id #uuid "6df2da19-269f-5bba-a866-2d28fc031ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65a0e4ce-bd6e-5296-8a0a-5fd18bf74b74" :answer/id #uuid "65a0e4ce-bd6e-5296-8a0a-5fd18bf74b74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-8}{4x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2c79c80-99de-54b9-9d82-c2f07cd702f0" :question/id #uuid "d2c79c80-99de-54b9-9d82-c2f07cd702f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343258" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})-1){y}^{′}+5y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?\n\n$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(x) & =(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2}))W(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c4ae727-1afb-5ef9-87af-f452ca62c1df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c4ae727-1afb-5ef9-87af-f452ca62c1df" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4ae727-1afb-5ef9-87af-f452ca62c1df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e61bd4ff-6144-5a7e-8e02-00c3e609c979" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e61bd4ff-6144-5a7e-8e02-00c3e609c979" "answer-9dae419f-7598-55b0-a2a6-b537e443ae0f" "answer-47d77792-7b25-57c9-bdc6-bc189048b501" "answer-29d77649-575e-537e-8070-76776b57eae2" "answer-db677ac0-7b00-5ae1-8c79-1afd9dadd6b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e61bd4ff-6144-5a7e-8e02-00c3e609c979" :answer/id #uuid "e61bd4ff-6144-5a7e-8e02-00c3e609c979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2}))W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dae419f-7598-55b0-a2a6-b537e443ae0f" :answer/id #uuid "9dae419f-7598-55b0-a2a6-b537e443ae0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})-1)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47d77792-7b25-57c9-bdc6-bc189048b501" :answer/id #uuid "47d77792-7b25-57c9-bdc6-bc189048b501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29d77649-575e-537e-8070-76776b57eae2" :answer/id #uuid "29d77649-575e-537e-8070-76776b57eae2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db677ac0-7b00-5ae1-8c79-1afd9dadd6b5" :answer/id #uuid "db677ac0-7b00-5ae1-8c79-1afd9dadd6b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-32e7120e-ecd0-54a1-8649-0fea9e5b153d" :question/id #uuid "32e7120e-ecd0-54a1-8649-0fea9e5b153d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343262" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?\n\n$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in standard form. Since $x>0$, we can divide both sides by ${x}^{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{3}{x}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{3}{x}W(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4ae4a21d-846d-5371-89fc-e2dd8e9af3e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4ae4a21d-846d-5371-89fc-e2dd8e9af3e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ae4a21d-846d-5371-89fc-e2dd8e9af3e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-00fd6574-74c6-5472-8ec2-afc12139c3ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5bd9306-b505-5e86-aab8-b589a392dc39" "answer-d9bbf0ae-9b58-5f81-baee-891729f34ee9" "answer-00fd6574-74c6-5472-8ec2-afc12139c3ab" "answer-44c5cc9a-98a5-502e-a69e-dbbe117ba10d" "answer-b5bf9e57-035f-5b67-9c47-089330d6eab6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5bd9306-b505-5e86-aab8-b589a392dc39" :answer/id #uuid "c5bd9306-b505-5e86-aab8-b589a392dc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3xW(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9bbf0ae-9b58-5f81-baee-891729f34ee9" :answer/id #uuid "d9bbf0ae-9b58-5f81-baee-891729f34ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00fd6574-74c6-5472-8ec2-afc12139c3ab" :answer/id #uuid "00fd6574-74c6-5472-8ec2-afc12139c3ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44c5cc9a-98a5-502e-a69e-dbbe117ba10d" :answer/id #uuid "44c5cc9a-98a5-502e-a69e-dbbe117ba10d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5bf9e57-035f-5b67-9c47-089330d6eab6" :answer/id #uuid "b5bf9e57-035f-5b67-9c47-089330d6eab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-64a84975-134c-59e7-b3de-faa7ec811813" :question/id #uuid "64a84975-134c-59e7-b3de-faa7ec811813" :question/math-academy-id "q-343254" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4){y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?\n\n$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(x) & =(4-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))W(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e650917-9c8c-5399-8075-d5c120d8aecb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e650917-9c8c-5399-8075-d5c120d8aecb" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e650917-9c8c-5399-8075-d5c120d8aecb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0fa976e1-3e6f-58f6-82a7-be56b4d82d06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0fa976e1-3e6f-58f6-82a7-be56b4d82d06" "answer-27c0ac50-87b6-504b-8aa2-8e7d4b4a7825" "answer-71ef6055-4626-5c9e-bf8c-d479b5bed105" "answer-3fc4c3e0-a11f-5140-bce9-cea64f5d6ae4" "answer-856e8138-9b56-52ff-9727-64cdd4f40c8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fa976e1-3e6f-58f6-82a7-be56b4d82d06" :answer/id #uuid "0fa976e1-3e6f-58f6-82a7-be56b4d82d06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27c0ac50-87b6-504b-8aa2-8e7d4b4a7825" :answer/id #uuid "27c0ac50-87b6-504b-8aa2-8e7d4b4a7825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71ef6055-4626-5c9e-bf8c-d479b5bed105" :answer/id #uuid "71ef6055-4626-5c9e-bf8c-d479b5bed105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fc4c3e0-a11f-5140-bce9-cea64f5d6ae4" :answer/id #uuid "3fc4c3e0-a11f-5140-bce9-cea64f5d6ae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856e8138-9b56-52ff-9727-64cdd4f40c8d" :answer/id #uuid "856e8138-9b56-52ff-9727-64cdd4f40c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-753b45d7-da51-5748-9817-073e29597daf" :question/id #uuid "753b45d7-da51-5748-9817-073e29597daf" :question/math-academy-id "q-343261" :question/problem "$$\n(x+1){y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?\n\n$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in standard form. Since $x>0$, we can divide both sides by $x+1$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{2x}{x+1}{y}^{′}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{x+1}y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2x}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2x}{x+1}W(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f054df8-5528-5182-a3c2-38d97e30f9c0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f054df8-5528-5182-a3c2-38d97e30f9c0" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f054df8-5528-5182-a3c2-38d97e30f9c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0342a05b-3acf-5c2d-a620-4ebb95fdb8e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0342a05b-3acf-5c2d-a620-4ebb95fdb8e2" "answer-033f2fdc-fe43-5a14-be7f-944d2c6065ac" "answer-12100e57-b84a-5582-a156-8cd0000a882d" "answer-1cb2fca6-0bdc-5251-bb05-7a59b21a0c82" "answer-c11b89d5-c585-5b5a-b4e4-4aab378e5779"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0342a05b-3acf-5c2d-a620-4ebb95fdb8e2" :answer/id #uuid "0342a05b-3acf-5c2d-a620-4ebb95fdb8e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{x+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-033f2fdc-fe43-5a14-be7f-944d2c6065ac" :answer/id #uuid "033f2fdc-fe43-5a14-be7f-944d2c6065ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12100e57-b84a-5582-a156-8cd0000a882d" :answer/id #uuid "12100e57-b84a-5582-a156-8cd0000a882d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cb2fca6-0bdc-5251-bb05-7a59b21a0c82" :answer/id #uuid "1cb2fca6-0bdc-5251-bb05-7a59b21a0c82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{x+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c11b89d5-c585-5b5a-b4e4-4aab378e5779" :answer/id #uuid "c11b89d5-c585-5b5a-b4e4-4aab378e5779" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317078 :answer-field/correct "answer-0d71e84b-d618-5a17-93c9-4e4987903896" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d71e84b-d618-5a17-93c9-4e4987903896"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d71e84b-d618-5a17-93c9-4e4987903896" :answer/id #uuid "0d71e84b-d618-5a17-93c9-4e4987903896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{-10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53cebc23-dff1-56fe-a57a-9a0d9ca25a96" :question/id #uuid "53cebc23-dff1-56fe-a57a-9a0d9ca25a96" :question/math-academy-id "q-343274" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+(1+x)y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(2)=5.$ What is $W(6)?$\n\n$W(6)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-3W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-3W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-3\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-3x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-3x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-3\\cdot 2} \\\\ 5 & =C{e}^{-6} \\\\ C & =5{e}^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=5{e}^{6}{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(6) & =5{e}^{6}{e}^{-3\\cdot 6}=5{e}^{-12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24ed920b-2433-56d0-bfb7-61417eb6d9c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24ed920b-2433-56d0-bfb7-61417eb6d9c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "24ed920b-2433-56d0-bfb7-61417eb6d9c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0157b7bd-12dd-5467-9e0b-69e6b3b508f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0157b7bd-12dd-5467-9e0b-69e6b3b508f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0157b7bd-12dd-5467-9e0b-69e6b3b508f7" :answer/id #uuid "0157b7bd-12dd-5467-9e0b-69e6b3b508f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{-12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa87e239-f514-5ab3-af2e-43a62163086f" :question/id #uuid "fa87e239-f514-5ab3-af2e-43a62163086f" :question/math-academy-id "q-343283" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}{y}^{′}+(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(0)=10.$ What is $W(2)?$\n\n$W(2)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}({x}^{2}+1)^{-1} \\\\ W & =\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=10$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =\\frac{C}{{0}^{2}+1} \\\\ 10 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =\\frac{10}{{2}^{2}+1}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d647e5a2-359a-5de6-8d63-fc0680cdce87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d647e5a2-359a-5de6-8d63-fc0680cdce87" :answer-field/id #uuid "d647e5a2-359a-5de6-8d63-fc0680cdce87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-85b13469-f244-5596-aa8e-0a73e70120fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85b13469-f244-5596-aa8e-0a73e70120fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85b13469-f244-5596-aa8e-0a73e70120fa" :answer/id #uuid "85b13469-f244-5596-aa8e-0a73e70120fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6daeb8c-1b8f-5fdd-ab26-f055c20928ce" :question/id #uuid "e6daeb8c-1b8f-5fdd-ab26-f055c20928ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-343290" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=5.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=5,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-1W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-2} \\\\ 5 & =C{e}^{-2} \\\\ C & =5{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=5{e}^{2}{e}^{-x}$ and $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e840763-0089-5eac-9b03-9edb709e1762" "answer-field-6d6975b2-cd8f-53c8-a76b-cbe26c306432" "answer-field-c9fa48ae-3277-50cc-aaef-292c47d4e634"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e840763-0089-5eac-9b03-9edb709e1762" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e840763-0089-5eac-9b03-9edb709e1762" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-245b91f9-9a34-52df-a77c-4058508e007b" :answer-field/choic